course: dictionary
lesson: 5180
title: Leaning letters: italic
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Italic is an adjective that describes printed letters which slope to the right, like handwriting. Look at this sentence: «Don't look back,» she told herself. The slanted letters are the italics, and the words she told herself are the clue that these are her private thoughts.
explain: Writers use italics for book titles, foreign words and words said with emphasis. In stories they often show thoughts or dreams. Italics is also a noun, usually in the plural, meaning those slanted letters themselves, as in «Check the italics in your title.»
explain: On a computer, press Ctrl+I (or Cmd+I on a Mac) to make your text italic. When you meet italic in a text, look at the words around it first. The context will tell you whether the writer means the slanted letters or the other meaning.
fact: Italic means printed letters that slope to the right, like handwriting.
fact: Italics is the plural noun for these slanted letters.
fact: In a story, italics often show a character's thoughts, as in «Don't look back,» she told herself.
fact: In computing, press Ctrl+I (or Cmd+I on a Mac) to make text italic.
fact: With a capital I, Italic can mean to do with ancient Italy and its peoples and languages.
exercise: «Don't look back,» she told herself. Why are these words in italics? | They show the page is torn | They show the story is about the weather | They show a number | *They show the character's own thoughts, not spoken words
exercise: In computing, which keys make text italic? | Ctrl+Z | *Ctrl+I (or Cmd+I on a Mac) | Ctrl+B | Shift+Enter
exercise: What does the noun «italics» mean? | Words said very loudly | A type of computer | *Printed letters that slope to the right | Letters that are bigger and bolder
test: Which word describes letters that slope to the right, like handwriting? | capital | bold | underline | *italic
test: In «Use italics for a book title», what are italics? | *Slanted letters used to show a title | Letters in a secret code | A kind of cloud | A type of pen
exam: Which is the best reason to use italics in a story? | To show the page number | *To show a character's thoughts, as in «Don't look back,» she told herself | To show the story is about the weather | To make the sentence longer
